From 7860efcf4daa6cdc0c95d3040a0196ce38ebd6d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:00:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] VACUNIT-1203: the Vacuum Unit window works on the PCIE-1203
 (ECAT-VC8 route, fail closed)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930: "vacuunit 所有功能按鈕和內部功能要有所對應，我需要實際上有功能" and
"針對1203 開啟 vacuunit 時，如果不符合現在程式碼就新創一個1203分支". Rulings the same day:
R1 there is no ECAT-VC8 on the ring today -- build it, fail closed, identity-check reads too;
R2 follow golden (tmr1Timer writes the threshold MODE at page open, no press);
R3 follow golden (SetIOTableByECAT_VC8_Sucker at boot, behind a #define, default ON).

The 1203 branch (every golden `#else` arm that had no 1203 code):
- VacuumUnit/Vc8Route.h (new): a POD route with function pointers, codes 0x7E0002xx, an inline
  slot. MyLaneIo GetIOValue / GetIOValueThread / SetIOValueThread and MyVacuumPanel
  RefreshDOIO / ReadVaccumIO / InitialThresholdMode use it in their `#else` arms. No route in the
  process = golden's own failure values (999.0, Error3 / Error5).
- EtherCAT/Pci1203Vc8.h (new): the ECAT-VC8 identity table (one row, name contains "ECAT-VC8",
  from golden rgVacuUnitType "ECAT-VC8_ODM1"), station / state / SDO address / value checks. A
  402 drive or any other module is refused with its real name, VendorID and ProductID.
- EtherCAT/Pci1203Vc8Route.inc (new, #included into Pci1203IoRoute.cpp): the route. Every entry
  checks the station first (ring 1, present, addressable, unique, the identity, the EC state);
  writes also need VacuUnitType==1, SystemStart and SoftStart false, the 1203 control armed, the
  DI/DO bytes in the card maps, and refuse vacuum-on while blow-on reads 1 (and the reverse).
  Every write is logged (console + oplog "VAC"), repeated refusals folded to once a minute.
  Installed from W906_InstallPci1203IoRoute (one writer, one call site; gate check 6).
- Pci1203Control: two internal kinds, kCmdVc8DoSet (DO channels 16..31 of that station,
  Acm_DaqDoSetBitEx from the card map) and kCmdVc8SdoWriteI16 (0x8000 + 0x10*vc, sub 0x02 = 1
  or sub 0x13 0..32767, DataSize 2), validated again inside Control; DRY RUN honoured.
- Pci1203Monitor::Vc8SdoReadI16: rate-limited threshold reads (16/s, back-off after 3 failures).
- Gates: control gate check 5e (VC8 SDO call sites: ring/station from the checked sample,
  literal subindex, vc_ bounded) with self-tests; SDO index table, 5d route files, 6 call sites;
  readonly gate lists the new write and read shapes. Both gates unchanged otherwise
  (readonly PASS; control: the same two pre-existing FAILs).

The window (FileRW/TestIF_File_VacuumUnit.cpp EOF, VacuumUnit/VacuumUnitLive.{h,inc}):
- WS vacuum.open / get {act:timer} / close (read; token-exempt) run golden FormShow + tmr1Timer
  (1 s while the page polls, only visible panels, threshold reads budgeted 8 a tick) on the live
  golden panels; vacuum.setSV / do / setAll / reset run golden btnSVClick /
  btnVaccumOnOffOnClick / btnSetInArmClick / sbResetClick. The ack lists every write
  (issued / DRY / refused / card error) and a snapshot with a per-panel reason.
- btnSetInArmClick is no longer gated: the Tags come from the DFM (btnSetInArm 0 /
  btnSetIndexArm 1 / btnSetOutArm 2, table asserted against the IR json), the web sends the arm
  by name. CLAUDE.md's "VacuumUnit.cpp:859-903 stays gated" is now stale.
- R3: SetIOTableByECAT_VC8_Sucker / SetSuckISABase / VaccumCopyFormSuck ported, run at boot when
  VacuUnitType==1 (golden main.cpp:10497-10498) under MachineType.h W906_VC8_SUCKER_REMAP
  (default ON; commented out = exactly today). The 144 sucker aliases are then switched / sensed
  only when their station is an ECAT-VC8 (W906_Vc8SuckerGate in MyLaneIo IOBitOn / IOBitOff /
  IOInputBit and the IO page's io.btnPanelClick): BTestSuck sits on ring 1 stations 0x50 / 0x51
  DO 16..19, the same channels as the loader / Auto1 cylinders.
- MachineType.h: only the new #define block is committed (index-only; the working copy's
  SOFT_SIMULTE edit is not part of this commit).

Deviations (each marked AI(W906-VACUNIT-1203) at the site): R4 only visible panels are read;
R5 SDO DataSize 2 (golden 128); D1 threshold reads budgeted; D2 DO read back every tick and after
a press; D3 vacuum-on and blow-on never both; D4 no writes while SystemStart / SoftStart;
edSet*Arm no longer read-only; vacuum.get / open / close exempt from the token.

Tests: tests/test_vacuum_vc8.cpp (ctest VacuumVc8, 119 / 119): the Set All table vs the DFM IR,
identity (a 32DI module at 0x50 is refused by name), no route / no VC8 = 999.0 / Error3 / Error5,
a fake VC8 (tick reads, the MODE written with no press, Set, Set All, ^ / v, the interlock),
the R3 remap and the sucker gate, the Control kinds being internal. build_integ_ship_x86_o2:
wb_serve + test_vacuum_vc8 build with no warning in the touched files; pe_truncation_check
PASS; macro_order_gate: no new site (4 pre-existing drifted rows in untouched files);
production_audit: 0 changes. Nothing was run against the card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
