+#  5e. THE ECAT-VC8 SDO WRITES ADDRESS THE STATION THAT PASSED THE IDENTITY CHECK,
+#      AND ONLY 8000h..8070h :02h / :13h.   AI(W906-VACUNIT-1203) 20260930.
+#
+#  kCmdVc8SdoWriteI16 (EtherCAT/Pci1203Control.cpp Vc8Issue_) is the first SDO write in
+#  this module aimed at RING 1 and at something that is not a drive. The index spelling
+#  alone (check 5) cannot say which station or which subindex, so for every call site
+#  whose index is the VC8 spelling this requires:
+#    * ring / station = (U16)v.ring, (U16)v.addr -- the monitor's slave sample that
+#      Vc8Validate_ proved is an ECAT-VC8 (EtherCAT/Pci1203Vc8.h), never a number from
+#      the caller;
+#    * the subindex = a literal 0x02 (threshold mode) or 0x13 (threshold);
+#    * `vc_ < 0 || vc_ > 7` within the 12 lines above -- so the index is 8000h..8070h.
+#  ⚠ On THIS machine golden's IndexArm2 stations 0x50 / 0x51 are DI / DO modules in OP;
+#    the identity check is what keeps these writes off them, and this is what keeps the
+#    call site tied to that check.
+# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+function Get-CallArgs([string]$text, [string]$fnRe) {
+    # $null when the call is not there or does not close; otherwise its top-level
+    # arguments, nesting respected (same rule as Get-SdoArg4).
+    $m = [regex]::Match($text, $fnRe)
+    if (-not $m.Success) { return $null }
+    $i = $m.Index + $m.Length
+    $depth = 0
+    $out = New-Object System.Collections.ArrayList
+    $sb = New-Object System.Text.StringBuilder
+    while ($i -lt $text.Length) {
+        $ch = $text[$i]
+        if ($ch -eq '(' -or $ch -eq '[') { $depth++ }
+        elseif ($ch -eq ']') { $depth-- }
+        elseif ($ch -eq ')') {
+            if ($depth -eq 0) { [void]$out.Add($sb.ToString().Trim()); return ,($out.ToArray()) }
+            $depth--
+        }
+        elseif ($ch -eq ',' -and $depth -eq 0) { [void]$out.Add($sb.ToString().Trim()); [void]$sb.Clear(); $i++; continue }
+        [void]$sb.Append($ch)
+        $i++
+    }
+    return $null
+}
